                <pb facs="0885" n="791" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg791"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.7131/100: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-06-06T14:00:00+01:44">June 6, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>13. Legation’s despatch 412, April 17th.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d742-f1"/>
                    Secretary General, Foreign Office informs me that in accordance with law voted
                    by Parliament proposals will shortly be made for exchange of notes providing for
                    indefinite extension of time for negotiation of commercial treaties not yet
                    concluded. Not even preliminary study of American draft proposal has yet begun
                    and I anticipate no action before late autumn owing to slow progress in
                    negotiations now in progress with neighboring and European countries.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
